# Docker build context excludes.
#
# CI runs `mvn -B verify` before `docker build`, so target/ now exists in the
# context. Everything in it is excluded except the one jar the `prebuilt` stage
# copies — otherwise classes/, test-classes/, surefire-reports/ and app.jar.original
# would all be uploaded to the builder and would bust the layer cache every run.
# The `build` stage is unaffected: it only needs pom.xml and src/.
target/*
!target/app.jar

# VCS, CI and agent metadata. Not needed to compile or run, and .git in particular
# changes on every commit, which would invalidate the context on every build.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.bolt
.idea
*.iml
qodana.yaml

# Docs and DB scratch files. The migrations Flyway actually runs are under
# src/main/resources/db/migration and stay in the context.
docs
database
README.md
SETUP.md
CLAUDE.md

# Stray Node bits at the repo root; this is a Maven project.
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json
index.js

# Local secrets must never end up in an image layer. Both imports in
# application.yml are `optional:`, so their absence is fine at build time —
# Render supplies these as env vars and /etc/secrets mounts at runtime.
src/main/resources/secrets.properties
.env

# Docker's own files are read by the client, not needed in the context.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
